From 85ece1f728dc420277d949a204f5309f0b868fcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: deepx-yjsong <yjsong@deepx.ai>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:17:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(infer,msgbroker,inputselector): expose silent drops
 as a `stats` structure

Each of these elements discards buffers while returning GST_FLOW_OK, so from
outside a frame dropped by design and a frame lost to a fault look the same.

Each element gets a read-only `stats` property (GstStructure, guint64 fields),
the convention of identity, rtpjitterbuffer and rtpsession: one read returns a
consistent snapshot, and a new counter does not change the API.

  dxinfer          application/x-dxinfer-stats
                   dropped-qos, dropped-throttled, dropped-no-meta,
                   dropped-after-eos
  dxmsgbroker      application/x-dxmsgbroker-stats
                   published, failed, no-message
  dxinputselector  application/x-dxinputselector-stats
                   pads-skipped

Counters reset when the element starts.

Tests: test_dxinfer_stats (new), and stats cases in
test_dxmsgbroker_failure_streak and test_dxinputselector_live_deadline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
